  "leadText": "Poverty, pain, and love: The country icon with the blonde wigs and the bright soprano voice has fallen silent. Millions see themselves in her songs and her story. What are they telling us?",
  "nzzSummaryEN": "- Dolly Parton, an iconic country music legend, has passed away at the age of 80; she wrote approximately 3,000 songs during her career, including major hits like \"Jolene\" and \"I Will Always Love You\".\n- Her career was defined by songs that narrate personal stories of poverty, pain, and love, showcasing her versatility in both country and pop genres with global recognition.\n- Other renowned works include songs like \"My Tennessee Mountain Home\", \"9 to 5\", and \"Islands in the Stream\", the latter created in collaboration with artists like Kenny Rogers.",
  "nzzSummaryDE": "Dolly Parton, a country music icon, has died at the age of 80. She wrote approximately 3,000 songs throughout her career, including several worldwide hits such as «Jolene» and «I Will Always Love You.» Her career was characterized by songs that told personal stories of poverty, pain, and love, and she achieved global recognition for her versatility in both the country and pop genres. Other well-known works include songs like «My Tennessee Mountain Home,» «9 to 5,» and «Islands in the Stream,» some of which were collaborations with other artists such as Kenny Rogers.",
  "nzzSummaryIsAuto": true,
